select $cv$Website Starter Collection$cv$, $cv$website-starter-collection$cv$, $cv$Four original website starter kits — business, service, portfolio and SaaS landing page — in one download.$cv$, $cv$A starter collection of original website layouts for business, portfolio, landing-page and service-based websites.$cv$, $cv$The Website Starter Collection brings together four of our original website starter kits so you can start a business site, a service company site, a personal portfolio or a software landing page from a solid, tested base.

Every kit is written in plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no frameworks and no build step: open the files, change the content and deploy to any static host. Each design has its own visual identity, a responsive layout, a keyboard-accessible mobile menu and colours controlled from a single block of CSS custom properties.

Included kits:
• Business Website Starter — home, about, services and contact pages with an FAQ accordion and a validated contact form.
• Service Business Starter — a one-page site for a home-services or consulting business with pricing-style service cards, a process section, service areas, an FAQ and a booking enquiry form.
• Portfolio Starter — a personal portfolio with filterable project cards, skills, an experience timeline, a case-study page and a light/dark theme toggle.
• SaaS Landing Page Starter — a landing page with a product UI mock, feature sections, a monthly/yearly pricing table, FAQ and a documented components page.

All copy, names and illustrations are original placeholders for you to replace. Contact and booking forms validate input in the browser and need a form service or your own backend to send messages — each README explains the options.$cv$, $cv$Template bundle$cv$,
  array[$cv$4 complete, original starter kits (10 HTML pages in total)$cv$, $cv$Business, service business, portfolio and SaaS landing page designs$cv$, $cv$Responsive layouts and accessible navigation in every kit$cv$, $cv$Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript — no build step$cv$, $cv$Rebrand each kit from one block of CSS variables$cv$, $cv$README with setup and customisation steps for each kit$cv$]::text[],
